<div class="page-content page-content--centered">
            <p><p><span style="font-size: small;">Jettribe is a true core Personal Watercraft brand that was born in Southern California in 1996. We&rsquo;ve lived, breathed and loved the sport since Kawasaki 550 stand-ups were king, neon and fluorescent colors were cool (the first time), and MC Hammer&rsquo;s &ldquo;running man&rdquo; was the move of all moves! We would dry off our mullets after every ride.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: small;">Though the times are a-changing, our mission has remained the same. With our passion and love for the watercraft industry and lifestyle, we aim to better the industry through our products and personal commitment. &nbsp;</span><br /><span style="font-size: small;">In the last few years, Jettribe has grown quite a bit and we owe every bit of it to the support and relationship of our fans, racers, dealers, distributors and overseas government institutions.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: small;">In 2014 Jettribe was totally grateful to be named as title sponsor of the 2014 IJSBA Jettribe World Finals at Lake Havasu City, Arizona. Plus, Jettribe is currently title sponsor of the "Best of the West" watercraft racing series in Southern California, as well as Title sponsor of the Jettribe European Race series, Jettribe Asia Invitational, Nordic Jetski Championship, and the official watercraft Gear of the Official Chinese and Thai race teams for the 2014 Asian Olympic Beach Games. &nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: small;">Plus, Jettribe is honored to be official partners CPL, Aquabike, Ruskky Grand Prix, and Martinique Off-Shore Race. </span><br /><span style="font-size: small;">&nbsp;</span><br /><span style="font-size: small;">In recent years we have really stepped up our game by having three Jettribe Race Rigs, running from California, Oregon  to Florida, our Jettribe Race Rig brings gear to the race fans and providing rider support at virtually every race and freeride event in the USA! Internationally, Jettribe has been taking our Jettribe USA Team overseas to China, Europe, Thailand, Russia, and Martinique. &nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: small;">We are truly stoked to have the biggest professional riders team line-up in the watercraft industry. Riders like Aqsa and Aero Aswar, Gyorgy Kasza, Erminio Iantosca, Kylie Ellmers, Anthony Torelli, Ryder Wildeboer, just to name a few! &nbsp;</span><br /><span style="font-size: small;">&nbsp;</span><br /><span style="font-size: small;">Stay tuned. There is always something happening at Jettribe Racing.</span><br /><br /><span style="font-size: small;">Jettribe has greatly contributed to the Personal Watercraft sport in China.&nbsp;&nbsp; We are involved in assisting our partners in China from gear to support staff for virtually every single PWC race in China. We are excited to help our partners grow this sport from its infancy to currently hosting international races. </span><br /><br /><span style="font-size: small;">To show our commitment to the sport, Jettribe formed the beginnings of the IJSBA (international Jet Sport Boat Association) in Vietnam&nbsp; - the VJSBA.&nbsp; This new association is now building interest for PWC racing in a whole new country.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p></p>
    </div>
